## 📌 Project Overview
Phishing remains one of the most critical threats in digital cybersecurity. This project implements an advanced text-classification pipeline engineered to distinguish malicious phishing attempts from legitimate corporate correspondence. The entire architecture—including email tokenization, vocabulary parsing, feature arrays, and multiple supervised classification models—was built independently from scratch using **NumPy** to ensure deep architectural comprehension.

## 🚀 Architectural Workflow (Built From Scratch)
- **Pre-processing Engine**: Programmed custom string parsers to lowercase text, remove structural layout footprints, isolate alphanumeric sequences, and filter out high-frequency stop words.
- **Feature Extraction**: Generated sparse structural matrix representations using vector tracking algorithms built manually to compute word densities.
- **Classification Engine**: Structured mathematical matrix iterations to train independent model variations.
- **Evaluation Pipeline**: Computed extensive validation arrays evaluating precision configurations to map and minimize dangerous classification oversights.

## 📊 Performance & Results
*Measured on a held-out stratified validation split of public benchmark datasets containing verified threat structures.*

| Model | Accuracy | Precision | Recall | F1-Score | ROC AUC |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **Naive Bayes Classifier** | [e.g., 0.9215] | [e.g., 0.9010] | [e.g., 0.9420] | [e.g., 0.9210] | [e.g., 0.9620] |
| **Logistic Regression** | [e.g., 0.9410] | [e.g., 0.9250] | [e.g., 0.9580] | [e.g., 0.9412] | [e.g., 0.9810] |
| **Support Vector Machine (SVM)** | [e.g., 0.9350] | [e.g., 0.9180] | [e.g., 0.9490] | [e.g., 0.9332] | [e.g., 0.9740] |

*(Note: Scikit-learn algorithms are imported strictly within the final testing script to act as an un-biased mathematical baseline validator).*

