## 🎯 High-Probability Campus Interview Questions
- **"Why is Recall the defining security metric for this project?"**: If the model flags a safe email as spam (False Positive), a user simply checks their junk folder. But if a malicious phishing email slips through unnoticed (**False Negative**), it opens the door to network compromise. Thus, maximizing **Recall** is critical.
- **"How did you mathematically handle the conditional probabilities in Naive Bayes from scratch?"**: Built a dictionary lookup framework inside NumPy to compute log-probabilities, preventing arithmetic underflow when multiplying long sequences of small floating-point decimals.
